#!/usr/bin/env perl
# PODNAME: skilletor
# ABSTRACT: Retired: the skilletor command of the CPAN distribution, now a notice
use strict;
use warnings;
use Skilletor::CLI;

exit Skilletor::CLI::run(@ARGV);

__END__

=pod

=encoding UTF-8

=head1 NAME

skilletor - Retired: the skilletor command of the CPAN distribution, now a notice

=head1 VERSION

version 0.009000

=head1 DESCRIPTION

This was the command of skilletor's Perl port, which is retired. Whatever it
is given, it prints a notice to standard error that says where to go instead
and exits 1; the C<hook> command, which the plugins run, exits 0. L<Skilletor>
names the replacement: the skilletor plugin for Claude Code, Codex or Hermes
Agent, or F<install.sh> for the command line,
L<https://github.com/Getty/skilletor#install>.

This last release of the distribution ships it as a stub, so an upgrade
replaces the earlier program.

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<Skilletor>, L<Skilletor::CLI>.

